#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lighting

#% text
# `lighting` is an option and a directive of 3D graphics that names the lights: a list of `ambient_light`, `directional_light`, `point_light` and `spot_light`, or `automatic`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The 3D renderer shades faces with its own fixed light; the option is accepted, so code written for other lighting runs, and is not used.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
graphics3d(sphere(), lighting: [ambient_light(gray), directional_light(white, [1, 1, 1])])
#% output
#= image("lighting.files/lighting-1.svgz")

#% cell
plot3d(sin(x + y), [x, 0, 3], [y, 0, 3], lighting: automatic)
#% output
#= image("lighting.files/lighting-2.svgz")

#% cell
graphics3d(sphere(), lighting: [point_light(red, [2, 0, 2])])
#% output
#= image("lighting.files/lighting-3.svgz")

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The picture is the same without it:

#% cell
graphics3d(sphere())
#% output
#= image("lighting.files/lighting-4.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `ambient_light`, `directional_light`, `point_light`, `spot_light`, `graphics3d`
